{id:"api-2014-magic-items-efreeti-bottle",name:"Efreeti Bottle",content:[{id:"Title",content:"Efreeti Bottle"},{id:"StatGrid",content:[{title:"Category",content:"Wondrous Items"},{title:"Rarity",content:"Very Rare"}]},{id:"TitledText",content:[{title:"",content:"Wondrous item, very rare"},{title:"",content:"This painted brass bottle weighs 1 pound. When you use an action to remove the stopper, a cloud of thick smoke flows out of the bottle. At the end of your turn, the smoke disappears with a flash of harmless fire, and an efreeti appears in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of you."},{title:"",content:"The first time the bottle is opened, the GM rolls to determine what happens."},{title:"",content:"| d100 | Effect |"},{title:"",content:"|---|---|"},{title:"",content:"| 01-10 | The efreeti attacks you. After fighting for 5 rounds, the efreeti disappears, and the bottle loses its magic. |"},{title:"",content:"| 11-90 | The efreeti serves you for 1 hour, doing as you command. Then the efreeti returns to the bottle, and a new stopper contains it. The stopper can't be removed for 24 hours. The next two times the bottle is opened, the same effect occurs. If the bottle is opened a fourth time, the efreeti escapes and disappears, and the bottle loses its magic. |"},{title:"",content:"| 91-100 | The efreeti can cast the wish spell three times for you. It disappears when it grants the final wish or after 1 hour, and the bottle loses its magic. |"}]}]}